net debt/EBITDA >3.0x, interest coverage <5x.\n3. **Recession/budget shock:** Public-sector and healthcare IT spending freezes \u2192 organic growth near zero \u2192 FCF margin <26% \u2192 value $300. Early warning: guidance cuts, order softness, state/federal budget delays.\n\n**Decision journal rule:** Re-evaluate on any quarterly miss of adjusted DEPS by >5%, net debt/EBITDA >3.5x, or close below $330 (bear-case value).\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 9. RED TEAM\n\n**Short thesis (same data):**\n1. AI-native entrants can collapse switching costs; Roper\u2019s niche vertical moats are less durable than their margins suggest.\n2. Net debt ~$9.05B and management adding buyback debt; with 10Y at 4.71%, leverage is not free.\n3. Adjusted DEPS excludes $0.9B annual acquisition amortization; the \"real\" P/E is higher than 18.6x.\n4. Q2 2026 GAAP net income included one-time/minority/beneficial-interest gains; TTM earnings are not sustainable.\n5. Revenue growth is partly acquisition-driven; organic growth ~5% does not justify a software premium.\n6. Institutional ownership 106% means forced-selling risk in ETF/redemptions.\n7. Market consensus targets ($440 mean/$420 median) imply only 2\u20137% upside \u2014 the market already knows this is \"fine.\"\n\n**Logic combat:**\n- Long logic score: 7/10\n- Short logic score: 6/10\n- Gap: 1 \u2192 Conviction capped at High, not Very High.\n\n**Killed arguments and validity conditions:**\n- \"AI destroys vertical software\" killed; would revive if churn >10% or renewal rates decline for 3 consecutive quarters.\n- \"Leverage is dangerous\" killed; would revive if net debt/EBITDA >3.5x and interest coverage <4x.\n- \"Low GAAP ROIC proves poor economics\" killed; Roper is an acquisition platform where incremental returns matter; would revive if incremental ROIC < WACC for 5 years.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\n**37-point audit summary:**\n- **Methodology:** Pass \u2014 Engine selection consistent with archetype; scenario distribution used; no DCF-only conclusion.\n- **Valuation:** Pass \u2014 Multiples cross-check, reverse DCF, sensitivity considered.\n- **Bias:** Pass with caveat \u2014 DCF single-point produced $583; scenario average $488; no overconfidence in point estimate.\n- **Consistency:** Pass \u2014 No mixing of core and optionality; no platform premium unbacked.\n- **Narrative:** Pass \u2014 qualitative statements quantified.\n- **Red team:** Pass \u2014 full adversarial section included.\n- **Data integrity:** Partial fail \u2014 segment detail and marketable securities unavailable; Q2 2026 one-time items classified [Unconfirmed]. This downgraded model confidence by 0.5 steps but did not invalidate conclusions.\n- **Re-calculations triggered:** None beyond the above confidence adjustment.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Date | 2026-08-24 |\n| T0 price | $411.79 |\n| Scenario-weighted IV | $488 |\n| Base-case IV | $490 |\n| Key assumption | Adjusted FCF base ~$2.45B; FCF margin 29.5%\u219230.5%; terminal g 3.5%; cost of equity 8.4% |\n| Red-team concern | AI moat erosion and leverage |\n| Data gaps | Segment detail; debt components; Q2 2026 one-time items; $3.2B buyback status [Unconfirmed] |\n| Decision | Buy/Accumulate, High conviction, target weight 7-8% |\n| Review trigger | Next quarterly earnings; organic growth and renewal commentary mandatory |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\n**Action:** **BUY / ACCUMULATE**\n**Conviction:** High (11/15)\n**Target weight:** 7\u20138% (use 7% if crowding score rises above 10/15)\n**Intrinsic value:** $488 (50% CI: $430\u2013$540)\n**Margin of safety:** ~15.6% (Adequate)\n\n**Entry strategy:**\n- Deploy 50% of intended position at market ($411.79)\n- Add 30% if price <$390\n- Add 20% if price <$360\n- Consider trimming if price >$540 and Thesis KPIs fail (organic growth <3%, churn >10%)\n\n**Sell/exit triggers:**\n- Net debt/EBITDA >3.5x with interest coverage <4x\n- Ch