nvention):\nPV of FY2026-FY2031 FCFs = 2.49 + 2.49 + 2.48 + 2.46 + 2.42 + 2.38 = $14.72B\nTerminal value = $3.54 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.075 \u2212 0.03) = $81.0B; PV = $52.5B\nEnterprise value = $67.2B\nEquity value = $67.2 + $0.3 (cash) \u2212 $11.0 (net debt) = $56.5B\nPer share (98.9M) = $571 [Estimate]\n\nMultiples cross-check at $571:\n\u2022 FY2026 adjusted DEPS $22.22 [Actual guidance midpoint-arithmetic] \u2192 25.7x\n\u2022 FY2027E adjusted EPS ~$24.3 (consensus +9.3% [Estimate]) \u2192 23.5x\n\u2022 FY2026E EV/EBITDA: $67.2 / $3.40 = 19.8x (historical 20-25x); not stretched.\n\u2022 PEG (trailing): 25.7 / 9.3 = 2.8 \u2014 optically expensive; PEG is the weakest bull\n  evidence and is a key red-team input.\n\nReverse DCF (what the market implies at $411.79):\nEV = $40.7 + $11.0 \u2212 $0.3 = $51.4B. With WACC 8.0%, TG 3.0%, FCF margin 30%,\nthe market implies total revenue growth of only ~2.5\u20133.0% in perpetuity \u2014 i.e. NO\ndurable M&A, NO real organic growth. That is far below management guidance of\n5% organic + recurring revenue growth of 7%. The market is pricing a broken-compounder\nscenario.\n\nTornado sensitivity (top 3 variables \u00b11\u03c3):\n1. WACC \u00b10.75pt (7.5% \u2192 6.75%/8.25%): IV \u2248 $665 / $485\n2. Total revenue growth \u00b11.5pt: IV \u2248 $640 / $475\n3. FCF margin \u00b11.5pt: IV \u2248 $610 / $530\n4. Terminal growth \u00b10.5pt: IV \u2248 $625 / $520\n5. Net debt \u00b1$2.0B: IV \u2248 $591 / $551\nTop-3 thesis KPIs: organic revenue growth, total revenue growth (M&A machine),\nWACC (rates/spread).\n\n\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3.5-1 Competitive response: If Roper's AI-enhanced vertical software regains 7%\norganic growth, large vertical-software consolidators (Constellation Software) and PE\nsponsors will bid up acquisition prices, eroding future IRRs. Impact: \u22121 [Assumption].\n\n3.5-2 Reflexivity: A weak Roper stock (down 24% from high) reduces management's\nacquisition currency (though deals are cash), weakens employee morale (SBC less\nvaluable), and invites activist attention. A strong stock would do the reverse.\nMagnitude: moderate. Current reflexivity is mildly negative.\n\n3.5-3 Customer behavior: Roper's niche vertical-software customers are\nmission-critical users with high switching costs; as penetration deepens, churn stays\nlow (vertical software renewal rates typically 88-93% [Estimate]) but new-customer\ngains slow. AI copilots could extend or disrupt this cycle \u2014 the key unknown.\n\n\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nScenario inputs derived from Sections 1.5 base rates, 3 (DCF), and 3.5 (second-order).\n\n| Scenario | Prob | Realization path | Key assumptions | IV |\n|----------|------|------------------|-----------------|----|\n| BEAR     | 25%  | Organic 4% \u2192 3.5%; M&A stalled at 3.3x leverage; AI disruption accelerates; FCF margin erodes to 28.5%; WACC 8.5%; TG 2.5% | DCF at WACC 8.5%, growth 4.5% \u2192 3.5%, TG 2.5% \u2192 IV $339 [Arithmetic] |\n| BASE     | 50%  | Organic 5-6% holds; M&A contributes 1.5-2.5% post-deleveraging; WACC 7.5%; TG 3.0%; FCF margin 30% | DCF as in Section 3 \u2192 IV $571 [Arithmetic] |\n| BULL     | 25%  | Organic 6-7%; AI becomes a tailwind/upsell driver; M&A re-accelerates in 2027; WACC 7.25%; TG 3.25%; FCF margin 30.5% | DCF at WACC 7.25%, growth 8% fading to 6%, TG 3.25% \u2192 IV $630 [Arithmetic] |\n\nExpected IV = 0.25\u00d7$339 + 0.50\u00d7$571 + 0.25\u00d7$630 = $527.75\nMargin of safety = ($527.75 \u2212 $411.79) / $527.75 = 22.0% \u2192 ADEQUATE (15\u201330%)\n50% CI: $430\u2013$620 | 80% CI: $340\u2013$700 [Assumption - derived from scenario spread]\n\nBayesian update (prior \u2192 posterior):\n\u2022 Prior (base rate): 35% probability a serial acquirer outperforms the market.\n\u2022 Evidence (likelihood ratio): raised FY2026 guidance twice; FCF +11% H1; buyback at\n  $356 avg; organic 5-6% for two quarters; Deltek softness flagged.\n\u2022 Posterior: ~45% probability of outperformance. We incorporate this by keeping Base\n  at 50% and Bear above pure base-rate (25%).\n\n\nSECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\u2022 Market-implied perpetual revenue growth: ~2.5\u20133.0% (reverse DCF, Section 3).\n\u2022 My horizon: 3\u20135 years at 5.5\u20137.5% total revenue growth (guided organic 5-6% +\n  modest M&A).\n\u2022 Spread: ~3pts of growth for ~5 years. If correct, the market's implied horizon is\n  effectively zero growth / no M&A \u2014 a materially pessimistic embedded assumption.\n\u2022 BUT: the spread can close by de-rating, not re-rating. Roper at 18.5x forward\n  earnings could go to 16x (bear) or 25x (bull). The arbitrage exists only if the\n  organic-growth KPI holds at \u22655%.\n\nSECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConviction score (15):\n1. Business quality: 3 \u2014 wide moat, stable 28% OPM, 30% FCF margins.\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 2 \u2014 22% MoS on probability-weighted IV; adequate,\n   not a deep value.\n3. Macro alignment: 1 \u2014 rates elevated/hawkish, late-cycle; headwind.\n4. Thesis clarity: 3 \u2014 KPIs measurable: organic growth, recurring revenue growth,\n   FCF/share, net debt/EBITDA, buyback pace.\n5. Execution traceability: 3 \u2014 12yr margin stability, guidance raised twice 2026,\n   $3.2B buyback demonstrates conviction.\nTOTAL: 12/15 \u2192 HIGH.\nAdjustments: Macro headwind \u22120.5 step; red-team logic gap (Section 9) \u22120.5 step.\nFinal conviction: HIGH (lower end).\n\nSizing: Conviction High \u2192 6\u20138% normal max. Macro headwind + leverage cap: \u22121pct.\nEngine 1 (no option cap). Final target weight: 5.0% (range 4\u20136%).\n\n\nSECTION 5.5 \u2014 