-----------------------------------------------------\n37-point audit summary:\nA. Methodology (7/7): Engine 1 appropriate; no DCF-only conclusion; multiples and\n   reverse DCF included; time horizons labelled T0/T-1/Tpf.\nB. Valuation (6/6): forecast drivers sourced; WACC derivation shown; terminal growth\n   \u2264 nominal GDP; tornado top-3 identified; data tags used.\nC. Bias (6/6): overconfidence checked \u2014 bull case is only 25% probability; base-rate\n   shock test passed; bear case is data-consistent; macro headwind applied.\n   ONE FAIL-WITH-CORRECTION: initial draft used vendor FCF without SBC; corrected to\n   owner earnings (OCF \u2212 capex \u2212 SBC).\nD. Consistency (6/6): share count T0 98.9M consistent with $3.2B buyback; net debt\n   11.0B consistent with FY2025 filed + H1 revolver drawings; no mixing of GAAP and\n   adjusted earnings.\nE. Narrative (5/5): no TAM-only language; no vague \"long-term potential\"; every\n   qualitative statement carries a number or [Assumption] tag.\nF. Red team (4/4): short thesis, logic combat, adversarial data consideration,\n   killed-argument conditions all present.\nG. Data integrity (6/6): capex discrepancy flagged; SBC series used from filings;\n   NI distortion flagged; [Unconfirmed] items not replaced with invented numbers;\n   earnings-call excerpt capped without Q&A acknowledged; vendor values marked.\nTOTAL: 40/40 checks pass (39 pass + 1 corrected before output). No recalculations\nrequired post-correction.\n\nSECTION 11 \u2014 DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDate: 2026-08-24\nT0 price: $411.79 | Shares: 98.9M | Market cap: $40.726B\nProbability-weighted IV: $527.75 | MoS: 22.0% | Conviction: HIGH (11/15)\nKey assumptions:\n\u2022 WACC 7.5% (rf 4.71% [Actual], ERP 4.5% [Assumption], beta 0.75 [Assumption])\n\u2022 FY2026 rev +8.9%, OPM 28.5%, FCF margin 30.0% [Actual guidance + arithmetic]\n\u2022 FY2027-31 revenue growth fade