u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nSECTION 0 \u2014 ANALYSIS OVERVIEW\n\n- Enterprise: Roper Technologies (ROP), a diversified compounder of vertical-market\n  software and technology-enabled niche products.\n- Archetype (Layer 0): B \u2014 Quality Compounder. Valuation engine: Engine 1\n  (Traditional DCF + Multiples).\n- T0 market capitalization: $40.726B [Aggregator, 2026-08-24]; using vendor shares\n  outstanding of 98.9M [Aggregator] \u2014 verified against filed data: Q1 2026 10-Q shows\n  102.4M shares outstanding at 2026-03-31 [Filed], and the Q2 2026 press release\n  (via Investing.com, [Estimate]) reports 4.3M shares repurchased at $1.5B in Q2;\n  102.4M \u2212 4.3M \u2248 98.1M, consistent with the vendor\u2019s 98.9M. Filed FY2025 weighted\n  average diluted shares of 108.2M [Filed] are an average for FY2025 and are NOT the\n  current count.\n- Headline TTM (through 2026-06-30): Revenue $8.280B [Filed], Net Income $2.504B\n  [Filed], OCF $2.669B [Filed], FCF $2.612B [Arithmetic].\n  CAUTION: Q2 2026 GAAP net income $1.169B [Filed] includes large one-time gains\n  (Indicor equity investment mark-to-market and Outgo beneficial interest \u2014 company\n  discloses these as non-GAAP adjustments [Q2 2026 press release via TradingView]).\n  Normalized TTM net income \u2248 $1.8B [Estimate].\n- Fair Value Estimate (Base Case): $510 per share.\n- Expected Value (Probability-Weighted): $481.50 per share.\n- Current price discount to Base Case IV: 19.3% (Adequate margin of safety).\n- Recommendation: BUY (Accumulate) on a 3-year horizon.\n- Target portfolio weight: 8% (7% after crowding adjustment), tranched entry.\n- Key monitoring KPI: organic revenue growth, enterprise gross retention,\n  net debt/EBITDA, adjusted DEPS vs guided midpoint.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 1 \u2014 MACRO CONTEXT\n\nSTEP 1-1 \u2014 MACRO VARIABLE CHECK\n- 10-Year Treasury yield: 4.65%\u20134.74% [Actual \u2014 FRED DGS10 2026-08-21 = 4.74%,\n  YCharts 2026-08-24 \u2248 4.65\u20134.71%]. Level HIGH and roughly FLAT/rising.\n- Real interest rates: 10Y TIPS-implied \u2248 1.7\u20132.1% [Estimate \u2014 4.7% nominal less\n  2.8\u20133.0% core inflation expectations]; restrictive for long-duration assets.\n- Fed policy stance: Federal funds target 3.50%\u20133.75% [Actual \u2014 Trading Economics,\n  FOMC July 2026: fifth consecutive hold; market prices ~1/3 probability of HIKE].\n  Stance: NEUTRAL-TO-TIGHTENING.\n- Dollar Index: [Unconfirmed \u2014 not retrievable in research budget]. Qualitative:\n  US rates at 3.50%+ during easing by other DM central banks implies DXY\n  supported. Assumed 98\u2013105 [Assumption].\n- Global liquidity: [Unconfirmed]. Constrained private credit is cited by Roper\n  management as improving M&A opportunities [Q1 2026 earnings call, Motley Fool\n  transcript].\n- Economic cycle position: LATE EXPANSION [Assumption \u2014 strong employment, sticky\n  inflation, Fed on hold with hike bias].\n- Inflation: [Estimate] \u2014 not retrieved directly; given Fed hold and market-priced\n  hike probability, assume core PCE 2.8\u20133.1%, above the 2% target.\n- Credit spreads: [Unconfirmed]. Roper\u2019s credit access remains tight to normal\n  (investment-grade; management notes constrained private credit for sellers,\n  which favors cash-rich acquirers).\n\nSTEP 1-2 \u2014 REGIME PROBABILITY DISTRIBUTION (MUST SUM TO 100%)\n- Goldilocks (disinflation + growth): 25%\n- Reflation (high rates + growth):   35%\n- Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 25%\n- Recession (low rates + low growth): 15%\nRationale: 10Y near 4.7%, Fed funds 3.50\u20133.75%, inflation sticky above target,\nbut labor and demand remain resilient enough that recession is a minority\nscenario.\n\nSTEP 1-3 \u2014 ENTERPRISE MACRO SENSITIVITY (EACH AXIS \u22123 TO +3)\n- Interest-rate sensitivity: \u22121 (long-duration software cash flows; but Roper\u2019s\n  mission-critical, short-contract recurring revenue is less rate-sensitive than\n  pure SaaS)\n- Dollar sensitivity: 0 (majority US revenue; some Europe/Asia exposure)\n- Liquidity sensitivity: +1 (cheap capital supports buybacks and M&A; tight\n  credit actually improves Roper\u2019s competitive position as a buyer)\n- Economic-cycle sensitivity: \u22121 (Technology-Enabled Products and DAT/ConstructConnect\n  have cyclical exposure; Application/Network software is defensive)\n- Commodity sensitivity: \u22121 (Neptune input-cost inflation; small overall)\n\nSTEP 1-4 \u2014 MACRO ALIGNMENT\nExpected Macro Impact = 0.25\u00d7(+) + 0.35\u00d7(0) + 0.25\u00d7(\u2212) + 0.15\u00d7(\u2212) \u2248 \u22120.4\nVerdict: NEUTRAL-TO-MILD HEADWIND. No conviction change; tranche entry retained.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 1.5 \u2014 BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\nSTEP 1.5-1 \u2014 BASE RATES\n- Quality compounder (Archetype B) 5-year survival: ~95%.\n- Vertical software portfolio with mid-90s gross retention remaining a going\n  concern after 5 years: ~85\u201390%.\n- Serial-acquirer compounder maintaining ROIC > WACC for 10 consecutive years:\n  ~30\u201340% \u2014 Roper is in the upper tail (12-year evidence below).\n- \u201cAI disruption\u201d of vertical software within 5 years (material margin erosion):\n  base rate ~15\u201325% given how mission-critical, compliance-heavy workflows\n  change slowly.\n\nSTEP 1.5-2 \u2014 DEVIATION FROM BASE RATE\n- Our weighted success probability (Base + Bull = 70%) exceeds the 50\u201360%\n  compounder base rate by ~1.2\u20131.4\u00d7. Three company-specific justifications:\n  1. 12 fiscal years of filed data (2014\u20132025) show operating margin never\n     outside a 23.1%\u201328.3% band [Filed], with FCF margin rising from 22.6% to\n     31.5% [Arithmetic].\n  2. Mid-90s enterprise gross retention, low-double-digit bookings growth\n     ex-price [Actual \u2014 company, Q1 2026 call], indicating pricing power and\n     switching-cost durability.\n  3. FY2026 adjusted DEPS guidance raised twice within five months\n     ($21.30\u201321.55 \u2192 $21.80\u201322.05 \u2192 $22.15\u201322.30 [Actual \u2014 company press\n     releases quoted via Grafa/TradingView/Investing.com]), consistent with\n     12-year guidance-accuracy record.\n\nSTEP 1.5-3 \u2014 BASE-RATE SHOCK CHECK\n- Success probability 70% vs base rate ~50%: ratio 1.4\u00d7 < 1.5\u00d7 threshold.\n- No Red Flag. No re-evaluation required.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY\n\nSTEP 2-1 \u2014 BUSINESS UNDERSTANDING\n- Roper acquires and operates ~25 vertical-market software and technology-enabled\n  product businesses across healthcare (Apex, Strata, CentralReach, SoftWriters),\n  government contracting (Deltek), construction (ConstructConnect), insurance\n  (Vertafore, iPipeline), legal (Aderant), education (Frontline), transportation\n  (DAT), and niche medical/industrial products (NDI, Verathon, Neptune).\n- Its decentralized model gives operating-company autonomy while headquarters\n  allocates capital (M&A, buybacks) and maintains an AI Accelerator to deploy AI\n  features portfolio-wide.\n- Revenue quality: recurring/reoccurring revenue \u2248 75% of total; Application\n  Software segment \u2248 85% recurring/reoccurring [Actual \u2014 Q1 2026 call].\nUnderstandability: HIGH.\n\nSTEP 2-2 \u2014 MOAT ASSESSMENT (0\u20133 each; total 21)\n1. Intangible assets: 2 (regulatory certifications, brand trust in niche verticals)\n2. Switching costs: 3 (mid-90s retention; workflow/data migration is painful)\n3. Network effects: 1 (DAT is a genuine two-sided freight marketplace; others limited)\n4. Cost advantage: 1\n5. Economies of scale: 2 (shared AI accelerator, centralized back office)\n6. Regulatory barriers: 2 (GovCon, healthcare compliance, insurance filings)\n7. Data moat: 2 (DAT loads, ConstructConnect project data, clinical data sets)\nMOAT SCORE: 13/21 \u2014 WIDE MOAT.\nMoat direction: WIDENING \u2014 evidence: AI-enabled features increase product\nstickiness (CentralReach 75% of new bookings AI-related [Actual \u2014 Q1 2026 call]);\nSaaS transitions deepen lock-in; bookings growth low-double-digits ex-price.\nNo evidence of narrowing: retention stable mid-90s, no churn acceleration.\n\nSTEP 2-3 \u2014 LYNCH CLASSIFICATION\n- FAST GROWER (portfolio of ~25 niche compounders growing 8\u201312% total revenue,\n  EPS 8\u201310%+).\n- Checkpoints: growth funded by retained FCF + manageable debt (no equity\n  dilution: shares outstanding DOWN from 108.2M FY2025 avg to 98.9M T0 [Actual]);\n  balance-sheet liquidity adequate ($297M cash + $3.5B revolver [Filed/Q1 2026\n  call]); business is understandable.\n\nSTEP 2-4 \u2014 FINANCIAL STRENGTH SCORECARD\n- Revenue growth, 3-yr CAGR: 13.7% [Arithmetic \u2014 FY2022\u2192FY2025; includes M&A].\n  TTM revenue growth: +10.9% [Arithmetic \u2014 TTM Q2 2026 $8.280B vs TTM Q2 2025\n  $7.469B].\n- Operating margin: 3-yr avg 28.3% [Arithmetic]; latest FY2025 28.3% [Filed];\n  12-yr median 28.0% [Arithmetic].\n- Adjusted EPS growth: FY2025 adjusted DEPS \u2248 $20.67 [Estimate \u2014 adjusted net\n  earnings $2.16B \u00f7 ~104.5M avg diluted shares] vs FY2023 ~$17.7 \u2192 CAGR \u2248 8.1%\n  [Estimate].\n- ROE (GAAP): 7.7% [Arithmetic \u2014 FY2025]; GAAP ROIC (incl. goodwill): 5.6%\n  [Estimate]; Adjusted ROIC (ex-goodwill): see Section 2.5.\n- FCF margin: FY2025 31.5% [Arithmetic]; FCF conversion (FCF/NI): 104% TTM\n  [Arithmetic].\n- Net debt/EBITDA: \u22482.7\u20133.1\u00d7 [Estimate \u2014 using $9.0B net debt \u00f7 ~$3.2\u20133.3B\n  adjusted EBITDA; company reported 3.1\u00d7 at Q1 2026 [Actual \u2014 call]].\n- Interest coverage: \u22485\u00d7 [Estimate \u2014 EBIT $2.235B \u00f7 est. interest $0.43\u20130.45B].\n- Net debt structure: Investment-grade; $3.5B revolver; term debt substantial.\n  Verdict: GOOD-TO-EXCELLENT.\n\nSTEP 2-5 \u2014 CAPITAL ALLOCATION SCORECARD (TOTAL 15)\n1. Buyback efficiency: 3/3 \u2014 6M shares (~5.5% of shares) repurchased Nov 2025 \u2013\n   Mar 2026 and 4.3M more in Q2 2026 [Actual \u2014 Q1 call; Investing.com estimate];\n   price range ~$330\u2013$400 vs. the stock\u2019s 5-yr average ~$450+; SBC ($166M FY2025\n   [Filed]) is far below buyback dollar volume.\n2. M&A track record: 3/3 \u2014 12-yr FCF CAGR 10.7% [Arithmetic, FY2020\u2192FY2025];\n   no material impairment flags in pack; Indicor creation (2022) and AMETEK\u2019s\n   reported $5B acquisition of Indicor instrumentation businesses [Estimate \u2014\n   TheNextWeb] imply Roper\u2019s 49% retained stake carries real optionality.\n3. Capex efficiency: 3/3 \u2014 capex/revenue 0.6% [Arithmetic]; maintenance-heavy\n   business requires almost no PP&E; incremental ROIC on software tuck-ins\n   historically >20% [Assumption \u2014 widely cited].\n4. Rationality of mix: 3/3 \u2014 management explicitly states \u201cunbiased between\n   acquisitions and opportunistic buybacks\u201d [Actual \u2014 Q1 2026 call]; a $3.8B\n   remaining buyback authorization coexists with an active proprietary M&A\n   pipeline.\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3/3 \u2014 FY2026 adjusted DEPS raised twice ($21.30\u201321.55 \u2192\n   $21.80\u201322.05 \u2192 $22.15\u201322.30 [Actual \u2014 company releases via secondary]);\n   prior track record consistent (FY2025 guidance raised to $19.90\u201320.05\n   [Estimate \u2014 Benzinga]).\nSubtotal: 15/15.\nInsider bonuses: Insider ownership 0.39% [Aggregator] \u2014 very low; NO bonus\npoint for >5% management ownership. Recent 6-month insider activity:\n[Unconfirmed]. No adjustment.\nFINAL CAPITAL ALLOCATION SCORE: 15/15.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\nSTEP 2.5-1 \u2014 R&D CAPITALIZATION\n- Roper\u2019s R&D/in-house software is small relative to revenue. Our filed capex\n  ($0.047B FY2025) excludes capitalized software, while the vendor\u2019s broader\n  capex ($0.105B) implies ~$0.058B of capitalized software [Estimate].\n  Capitalizing $0.058B as a 3-yr asset changes operating income by <10bps.\n  IMMATERIAL.\n\nSTEP 2.5-2 \u2014 SBC PROPER TREATMENT\n- FY2025 SBC: $0.166B [Filed]. Owner FCF = Reported FCF \u2212 SBC =\n  $2.493B \u2212 $0.166B = $2.327B [Arithmetic].\n- All forward FCF forecasts below are AFTER-SBC.\n- Share-count treatment: current shares 98.9M [Aggregator \u2014 corroborated by\n  filed share-count decline]; buybacks have overwhelmed SBC dilution by ~8:1\n  in 2026 [Estimate \u2014 6M+4.3M bought vs ~1M issued].\n\nSTEP 2.5-3 \u2014 OPERATING LEASE CAPITALIZATION\n- FY2025 operating leases: $0.234B [Filed]. Capitalized at 8\u00d7: +$1.9B debt;\n  Adjusted net debt = $9.0B + $1.9B = $10.9B [Estimate]. Net debt/EBITDA still\n  \u22483.3\u00d7 \u2014 leverage remains manageable. (Lease capitalization NOT included in\n  headline net debt; disclosed here as a sensitivity.)\n\nSTEP 2.5-4 \u2014 BRAND/DATA ASSET ESTIMATION\n- Not reliably market-valued. DAT, ConstructConnect, and clinical datasets are\n  strategically important but [Unconfirmed] as separable fair values.\n  No premium added to EV.\n\nSTEP 2.5-5 \u2014 ADJUSTED ROIC\n- GAAP invested capital = Total assets \u2212 current liabilities \u2212 cash =\n  $34.577B \u2212 $3.726B \u2212 $0.297B = $30.554B [Arithmetic].\n- Excluding accumulated acquisition goodwill (est. $18\u201320B [Assumption based\n  on large acquisition history]): Adjusted IC \u2248 $10.5\u201312.5B.\n- Adjusted NOPAT \u2248 $1.70B [Arithmetic \u2014 EBIT $2.235B \u00d7 (1\u221224%)]; Owner FCF\n  $2.327B [Arithmetic].\n- Adjusted ROIC (on Owner FCF): 2.327 / ~11.5 = ~20% [Estimate].\n- GAAP vs Adjusted ROIC gap \u2248 15%p \u2014 fully explained by acquisition goodwill.\n\nSTEP 2.5-6 \u2014 OWNER EARNINGS (BUFFETT STYLE)\n- FY2025: NI $1.536B [Filed] + D&A $0.898B [Filed] \u2212 maintenance capex ~$0.05B\n  [Filed] \u2212 \u0394WC (+$0.492B increase, use of cash) [Arithmetic] = $1.892B [Arithmetic].\n- The \u0394WC swing is lumpy; on a 3-yr average, owner earnings \u2248 $2.1\u20132.2B\n  [Estimate].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE 1: TRADITIONAL DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\nDISCOUNT RATE DERIVATION (WACC)\n- Risk-free rate: 4.70% [Actual \u2014 FRED DGS10 2026-08-21 4.74%; YCharts 4.65\u20134.71%.\n  Using 4.7%].\n- Equity risk premium: 4.75% [Assumption \u2014 standard long-horizon ERP in 2026\n  environment].\n- Beta: 0.85 [Assumption \u2014 vendor beta 0.737 [Aggregator] is unverified and\n  likely understates risk given 3.1\u00d7 net leverage and the AI-disruption debate;\n  an 0.85 levered beta is conservative for a defensive compounder].\n- Cost of equity: 4.7% + 0.85 \u00d7 4.75% = 8.74%.\n- Pre-tax cost of debt: 4.8% [Assumption \u2014 investment-grade spread ~130bps over\n  SOFR 3.5%].\n- Marginal cash tax rate: 24% [Assumption \u2014 FY2022\u20132025 normalized effective rate].\n- After-tax cost of debt: 3.65%.\n- Capital structure: E = $40.7B [Arithmetic]; D = $9.3B [Estimate \u2014 see net debt\n  below]; E/(D+E) = 81.4%; D/(D+E) = 18.6%.\n- WACC = 0.814 \u00d7 8.74% + 0.186 \u00d7 3.65% = 7.80%.\n\nNET DEBT (JUDGMENT CALL, COMPONENTS DECLARED)\n- Selected components: LONG-TERM DEBT $8.596B [Filed FY2025] + CURRENT PORTION\n  $0.705B [Filed FY2025] \u2212 CASH $0.297B [Filed FY2025] = $9.004B \u2192 $9.0B\n  [Estimate].\n- Cross-check: vendor total debt $9.349B [Aggregator]; net debt \u2248 $9.05B \u2014\n  immaterial difference. Operating leases (+$1.9B if capitalized) shown as\n  sensitivity only.\n\nEXPLICIT FORECAST (ALL FORECAST DRIVERS SOURCED)\nRevenue ($B) | FCF margin | Owner FCF ($B) | Source/driver\nFY2026E: 8.55 | 30.0% | 2.57 | Revenue = 8% guided growth [Actual \u2014 Q1 2026 call\n  reiterated ~8% total, 5\u20136% organic] on FY2025 $7.902B [Filed]; H1 2026 run-rate\n  $4.204B [Filed] implies H2 ~$4.35B. FCF margin = FY2025 29.4% [Arithmetic] +\n  modest mix improvement; TTM margin 31.5% [Arithmetic]. 30.0% is conservative\n  [Assumption].\nFY2027E: 9.15 | 30.0% | 2.75 | Revenue +7.0% [Assumption \u2014 consensus 2027E\n  revenue \u2248 $9.09B [Estimate \u2014 Yahoo Finance]; management organic guide at\n  5\u20136%; M&A adds ~1\u20132%. We use 7.0% (self-side consensus 8.8% is optimistic)].\n  FCF margin 30.0% [Assumption \u2014 stable].\nFY2028E: 9.74 | 30.0% | 2.92 | Revenue +6.5% [Assumption \u2014 fade to high-organic,\n  low-M&A]. Margin 30.0% [Assumption].\nFY2029E: 10.33 | 30.5% | 3.15 | Revenue +6.0% [Assumption]. Margin 30.5%\n  [Assumption \u2014 software mix shift (TEP shrinks) aids margin].\nFY2030E: 10.90 | 30.5% | 3.32 | Revenue +5.5% [Assumption]. Margin 30.5%.\nFY2031E: 11.44 | 30.5% | 3.49 | Revenue +5.0% [Assumption]. Margin 30.5%.\nTerminal growth: 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 long-run nominal GDP; below WACC].\n- Capex embedded: $0.05\u20130.07B/yr [Assumption \u2014 consistent with FY2025 $0.047B\n  [Filed]).\n- SBC embedded: $0.18\u20130.22B/yr [Assumption \u2014 FY2025 $0.166B [Filed] + modest\n  growth).\n- D&A (for informational bridge): $0.95B FY2026E growing ~5%/yr [Assumption \u2014\n  FY2025 $0.898B [Filed] plus acquisition amortization].\n\nDISCOUNTED CASH FLOW (WACC 7.8%)\nYear | FCF ($B) | Discount factor | PV ($B)\nFY2026 | 2.57 | 0.928 | 2.38\nFY2027 | 2.75 | 0.861 | 2.36\nFY2028 | 2.92 | 0.799 | 2.34\nFY2029 | 3.15 | 0.741 | 2.34\nFY2030 | 3.32 | 0.687 | 2.28\nSum explicit PV = 11.70\nTerminal value = 3.49 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.078 \u2212 0.03) = 74.87\nPV of terminal value = 74.87 \u00d7 0.638 = 47.77\nENTERPRISE VALUE = $59.47B\n\u2212 Net debt $9.00B\nEQUITY VALUE = $50.47B\nINTRINSIC VALUE PER SHARE = $50.47B / 98.9M = $510 [Estimate]\n\nSENSITIVITY (TORNADO, \u00b11\u03c3)\n- WACC \u00b10.5%: IV range $456 (8.3%) to $571 (7.3%) \u2014 MOST SENSITIVE.\n- Terminal growth \u00b10.5%: IV range $452 (2.5%) to $584 (3.5%).\n- FCF margin \u00b11.5%: IV range $466 to $553.\nTop-3 variables: WACC, terminal growth, FCF margin. These are the thesis KPIs.\n\nMULTIPLE CROSS-CHECKS (NO DCF-ONLY CONCLUSION)\n- P/E: Current price / FY2026E adjusted DEPS $22.22 [Actual \u2014 guidance midpoint]\n  = 18.5\u00d7; IV of $510 = 23.0\u00d7. Historical Roper trade range: 20\u201328\u00d7 [Estimate \u2014\n  TIKR Nov 2025 cites 21.1\u00d7 forward as current market; history from observed\n  multi-year behavior]. Fair multiple for 8\u201310% EPS growth with mid-90s\n  retention: 20\u201323\u00d7 [Assumption].\n- EV/EBITDA: FY2026E adjusted EBITDA \u2248 $3.35B [Estimate \u2014 margin ~39.2%;\n  Q1 2026 actual EBITDA $797M [Actual]]. Current price EV/EBITDA = 14.8\u00d7;\n  IV EV/EBITDA = 17.7\u00d7. Historical range 18\u201324\u00d7 [Assumption].\n- P/FCF: Current P/Owner-FCF (FY2026E) = 15.9\u00d7; IV = 19.6\u00d7. Historical\n  25\u201335\u00d7 \u2192 current multiple is the LOWEST in the modern franchise era.\nCONCLUSION: Engine 1 \u2192 IV $510 (range $450\u2013570). Multiple analysis supports.\nNo peer-only or TAM-only conclusions made.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n1. Competitive response: If Roper\u2019s AI suite succeeds, vertical-software peers\n   (Constellation, IHS, specialty incumbents) will replicate features. Impact:\n   \u22121 (small negative). Roper\u2019s data density and workflow lock-in provide\n   defensibility.\n2. Reflexivity: Positive loop \u2014 sustained buybacks at low multiples increase\n   EPS growth, attracting fund flows; high share price also enables low-cost\n   acquisition currency. As of T0, buybacks are large and reflexive.\n3. Customer evolution: Early-adopter \u2192 mainstream transition in vertical\n   software favors Roper: SaaS conversion (2\u20132.5\u00d7 uplift over 5\u201310 years,\n   50\u2013100bps annual growth [Actual \u2014 Q1 2026 call]) deepens customer value.\n   Penetration is moderate; no exhaustion of TAM evident.\nNet second-order effect: NEUTRAL-to-SLIGHTLY-POSITIVE.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nSTEP 4-1/2 \u2014 SCENARIO SET\nSCENARIO | PROB | PRICE 3YR | PER-SHARE THESIS\nBull | 25% | $600 | Organic 6.5%+, AI features monetize at scale, M&A adds\n  2\u20133%, WACC 7.4%, TG 3.2%; multiple expands to 24\u00d7 FY2027E EPS; Indicor exit\n  distributes cash.\nBase | 45% | $510 | Organic 5\u20136%, M&A ~2%, FCF margin ~30%, WACC 7.8%,\n  TG 3.0%; multiple reverts to 20\u201321\u00d7 adjusted EPS.\nBear | 25% | $360 | Organic 4%, M&A 1%, FCF margin 27.5%, WACC 8.5%, TG 2.5%;\n  AI discount persists, multiple compresses to 15\u201316\u00d7; leverage stays 3\u00d7.\nSevere Bear | 5% | $240 | Recession + AI disruption of retention + acquisition\n  misstep; multiple 12\u00d7; net debt/EBITDA > 4\u00d7.\nTOTAL = 100%.\n\nSTEP 4-3 \u2014 BAYESIAN UPDATE\n- Prior (Layer 1.5): compounder success (positive 5-yr real return) ~55%.\n- Update signals: FY2026 guidance raised twice [Actual]; Q2 2026 GAAP EPS\n  $11.62 [Actual] (headline distorts \u2014 recurrence skepticism warranted);\n  buyback 8%+ of shares in 9 months [Actual]; retention mid-90s [Actual].\n- Posterior: Bull+Base = 70% (vs prior 55%). Likelihood ratio \u2248 1.3 \u2014 justified\n  by concrete company-specific confirmation.\n\nSTEP 4-4/5 \u2014 EXPECTED PRICE & MARGIN OF SAFETY\n- Expected 3-yr price = 0.25\u00d7600 + 0.45\u00d7510 + 0.25\u00d7360 + 0.05\u00d7240 = $481.50.\n- 50% CI: $400\u2013530. 80% CI: $300\u2013590.\n- Margin of Safety vs Base IV $510: (510 \u2212 411.79) / 510 = 19.3% \u2192 ADEQUATE.\n- Expected 12-month total return \u2248 ($481.50 + $3.79 dividend) / $411.79 \u2212 1\n  \u2248 +17.9%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\n- Market-implied horizon: at $411.79 on FY2026E adjusted EPS of $22.22, the\n  market pays 18.5\u00d7 \u2014 implying ~5\u20136 years of discounted earnings at 9\u201310%\n  growth, with no terminal premium. That is a SHORT horizon for a compounder\n  with 95% retention and a 20-year runway in vertical software.\n- Our horizon: 3\u20135 years explicit + terminal; we capitalize a 3% terminal\n  growth beyond FY2031.\n- Spread: ~1\u20132 years. MODEST arbitration exists, not extreme.\n- Implication: this is a \u201cfair-to-slightly-cheap\u201d compounder, not a deep-value\n  special situation.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\nSTEP 5-1 \u2014 CONVICTION SCORE (0\u201315)\n1. Business Quality: 3/3 (Wide moat, 95% retention, 28% operating margin x 12 yrs)\n2. Valuation Attractiveness: 2/3 (19% MoS; historical-low multiple but not\n   distressed)\n3. Macro Alignment: 2/3 (Neutral-to-mild headwind due to high rates)\n4. Thesis Clarity: 3/3 (Measurable KPIs: organic %; adjusted DEPS;\n   net debt/EBITDA; retention; bookings)\n5. Execution Traceability: 3/3 (12 years of filed data; guidance raised twice\n   in 2026; capital allocation score 15/15)\nCONVICTION = 13/15 \u2192 VERY HIGH.\nSTEP 5-2 \u2014 CONVICTION DECAY: \u22121 point every 6 months absent confirming evidence.\nSTEP 5-3 \u2014 SIZING GUIDELINE: Very High \u2192 target 8\u201310%; Macro-neutral \u2192 7\u20138%;\nCrowding (below) \u2192 7\u20138%. Final target: 8%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5.5 \u2014 BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n- Short interest: 6.25% of float, 5.38M shares, 5.89 DTC, MoM \u22126.8%\n  [Aggregator \u2014 2026-08-14]. Moderate; short pressure unwinding (supportive).\n- Institutional ownership: 106.84% [Aggregator \u2014 13F double-counting includes\n  ETFs]. VERY HIGH \u2014 vulnerable to software-sector ETF outflows.\n- Insider: 0.39% [Aggregator]. Low skin-in-game; not a positive signal.\n- Options positioning: [Unconfirmed \u2014 not retrievable].\n- Sentiment extreme: price \u221224% from 52-wk high $544.94; price target mean\n  $440.25, median $420, low $335, high $550 [Aggregator]. Sentiment is\n  CAUTIOUS \u2014 not yet capitulation.\n- Crowding Risk Score: 7/15 \u2014 high institutional ownership, moderate short\n  interest, cautious sell-side. Requires position-size haircut of ~0.5\u20131%p.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT\n\n- ROP provides low-beta (0.74\u20130.85) defensive FCF, a small dividend (yield\n  0.92% [Aggregator]), and negative correlation to deep cyclicals.\n- In a portfolio with mid-to-late-cycle value holdings, ROP improves portfolio\n  Sharpe; in a portfolio already heavy in software/tech/growth, it adds\n  correlation risk.\n- Expected portfolio effect: ADD (diversifier) with a hard cap of 10% single-name.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING\n\n- Binary-expected return structure:\n  Win scenarios (70%): weighted gain +26.0%.\n  Lose scenarios (30%): weighted loss \u221217.4%.\n- Odds b = 26.0 / 17.4 = 1.49.\n- Kelly f* = (0.70 \u00d7 1.49 \u2212 0.30) / 1.49 = 49.8%.\n- Half-Kelly = 24.9%.\n- Practical cap (single-name, crowding-adjusted, macro-neutral) = 8\u201310%.\n- RE-ANALYSIS REQUIRED: Layer 5 (8%) vs Layer 6.5 half-Kelly (24.9%) gap =\n  16.9%p. The gap is resolved by: (i) 80% CI lower bound of $300 (\u221227%), a fat\n  left tail that binary Kelly underweights; (ii) 106.84% institutional crowding;\n  (iii) 3.1\u00d7 leverage; (iv) AI-disruption ambiguity; (v) the pack\u2019s non-zero\n  [Unconfirmed] data weight. FINAL SIZE: 8% target, 10% hard cap.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\nPRIMARY RISKS (probability, impact)\n1. AI disruption of vertical-software workflows (P 20%, I \u221245% to IV $380):\n   agents replace project-data, freight-matching, or compliance tasks.\n   Mitigant: Roper is an early deployer of AI features; enterprise retention\n   mid-90s [Actual].\n2. Leverage/capital-allocation accident (P 15%, I \u221230%): >$10B acquisition at\n   peak multiples or leverage > 4\u00d7. Mitigant: capital allocation score 15/15;\n   management emphasizes discipline [Actual \u2014 Q1 call].\n3. Rate shock: 10Y > 5.2% (P 25%, I \u221220% to IV $410). Mitigant: low-duration\n   mission-critical revenue base.\n4. TEP segment cyclicality/input-cost inflation (P 30%, I \u22125%).\n5. Institutional-outflow cascade from software-sector de-rating (P 25%,\n   I \u221215% short-term).\n\nCATALYSTS (probability, impact)\n1. Raised guidance again (P 35%, +10%): FY2026 exit at high end of $22.15\u201322.30.\n2. AI feature monetization becomes visible in organic growth (P 40%, +10\u201315%).\n3. Accelerated buybacks with remaining $3.8B authorization (P 50%, +5\u201310%):\n   8\u201310% of shares could be retired at current prices.\n4. M&A pipeline conversion (proprietary, seller-financially-distressed) (P 30%,\n   +10%).\n5. Indicor monetization / special dividend (P 20%, +5\u20137%; Indicor stake value\n   [Unconfirmed] but AMETEK\u2019s reported $5B deal [Estimate \u2014 TheNextWeb] implies\n   a meaningful Roper cash-out).\n\nPRE-MORTEM (MANDATORY)\n\u201cIf ROP fails to produce a positive 5-year return from today, the most likely\ncauses are:\u201d\n1. AI-native competitors disintermediate workflow software; retention drops\n   below 90%; organic growth \u2192 0\u20132%. Early-warning indicators: gross retention\n   < 92%; bookings growth negative; organic revenue < 3%.\n2. Management does a transformative debt-funded acquisition that destroys\n   ROIC; goodwill impairments follow. Early-warning indicators: net debt/EBITDA\n   > 3.5\u00d7; deal size > $10B; adjusted EBITDA margin guidance cut.\n3. A persistent 10Y > 5.5% environment compresses all long-duration assets;\n   ROP trades at 14\u00d7 despite stable fundamentals. Early-warning indicators:\n   10Y > 5%; software sector median EV/EBITDA < 14\u00d7.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\n- Common bear trigger with other software/growth holdings: rising 10Y yields.\n  If the portfolio holds high-multiple tech, ROP adds substantial tail\n  correlation \u2014 the 2022 playbook shows software de-rating as a shared shock.\n- Conditional VaR (5%, 12-month): severe-bear scenario $240 \u2248 \u221241.7%.\n  Blended 5\u201310% CVaR \u2248 \u221225% to \u221230% [Estimate].\n- Portfolio mitigation: pair ROP with financial/energy cyclicals; cap combined\n  long-duration tech exposure at 30% of portfolio.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES\n\nTHESIS INTEGRITY CRITERIA (RE-EVALUATION TRIGGERS)\n- KPI 1: ORGANIC REVENUE GROWTH. Threshold: >4.5% quarterly.\n  Breach: if <4% for two consecutive quarters \u2192 re-evaluate base case.\n- KPI 2: ENTERPRISE GROSS RETENTION. Threshold: \u226593%.\n  Breach: <92% \u2192 downgrade moat rating; cut weighting.\n- KPI 3: ADJUSTED DEPS vs GUIDANCE. Threshold: within guided range.\n  Breach: full-year miss or guidance withdrawal \u2192 conviction \u22122 steps.\n- KPI 4: NET DEBT/EBITDA. Threshold: \u22643.2\u00d7.\n  Breach: >3.5\u00d7 \u2192 reduce target weight 2%p.\n- KPI 5: FCF CONVERSION (Owner FCF/adjusted net earnings). Threshold: \u22650.95\u00d7.\n- KPI 6: 10-YEAR TREASURY. If >5.2%, review valuation model at WACC 8.5%+\n  (IV \u2248 $456).\n- KPI 7: SHARE COUNT. Monthly buybacks should keep shares \u226499M; if shares\n  increase, question capital allocation.\n\nQUARTERLY REVIEW DISCIPLINE\n- First Friday after 10-Q: update guidance, segment margins, M&A spending,\n  retention, bookings.\n- Annual: re-run DCF with updated WACC components and 5-yr guidance picture.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\nSTEP 9-1 \u2014 SHORT THESIS (SAME DATA)\n1. Organic growth of 5\u20136% is barely above nominal GDP; \u201cgrowth\u201d is mostly\n   M&A financed with 3.1\u00d7 leverage, and adjusted EPS growth (~8%) is flattered\n   by 9% share retirement that cannot persist at this pace.\n2. AI is a structural threat to workflow software fees: if an agent can run\n   RFPs (ConstructConnect), insurance quotes (Vertafore), or fleet dispatch\n   (DAT), Roper\u2019s per-seat pricing erodes \u2014 and its moat (vertical data) is\n   being commoditized by foundation-model providers.\n3. FCF quality qualifier: OCF adds back SBC ( $166M FY2025 [Filed]) and the\n   TTM FCF of $2.612B includes working-capital tailwinds that may reverse.\n   True owner FCF \u2248 $2.33B [Arithmetic].\n4. Q2 2026 GAAP EPS $11.62 [Actual] includes large non-recurring gains; naive\n   consensus extrapolation will reverse, creating negative earnings momentum.\n5. Technology-Enabled Products (~25\u201330% of revenue) is a cyclical industrial\n   remnants business with thin moats and input-cost inflation (Neptune).\n6. At $411.79, the stock has already lost 24% of its value; mean price target\n   $440 [Aggregator] caps upside; momentum is negative.\n7. Institutional ownership 106.84% means no incremental buyer left; any ETF\n   outflow accelerates declines.\n\nSTEP 9-2 \u2014 LOGIC COMBAT (LONG vs SHORT)\n- Long strength: 7/10 \u2014 supported by 12 years of filed financials, stable\n  margins, improving capital returns, real (not narrative) FCF.\n- Short strength: 5/10 \u2014 AI disruption is plausible but unproven; current\n  retention and bookings contradict it; \u201cEPS flattery\u201d argument is partially\n  true but priced in at 18.5\u00d7.\n- GAP = 2 \u2192 NO CONVICTION DOWNGRADE required (had the gap been <2, conviction\n  would drop to 11).\n\nSTEP 9-3 \u2014 ADVERSARIAL REFERENCES\n- Seeking Alpha: \u201cWide Moat, Rising Debt, and Narrowing Upside\u201d; \u201cMoat Under\n  Threat as AI Threatens Vertical Software\u201d [Estimate \u2014 cited in research\n  brief]. Both identified debt and AI as core vulnerabilities.\n- No Hindenburg-type short report flagged in retrievable sources as of\n  2026-08 [Unconfirmed].\n\nSTEP 9-4 \u2014 KILLED ARGUMENTS AND RE-ARMING CONDITIONS\n1. \u201cRoper is a roll-up that will eventually hit an integration wall.\u201d\n   Killed by 12 years of stable margins and FCF conversion.\n   Re-arms if: management does a >$10B acquisition or net debt/EBITDA > 4\u00d7.\n2. \u201cAI makes Roper obsolete.\u201d Killed by mid-90s retention, low-double-digit\n   bookings, and emergent AI monetization (75% of CentralReach new bookings).\n   Re-arms if: gross retention < 90% for 2 consecutive quarters.\n3. \u201cGAAP net income is stagnant.\u201d Killed by 2022 one-time tax benefit and\n   2026 one-time gains; adjusted earnings have grown every year.\n   Re-arms if: adjusted EBITDA margin declines > 200bps in a year.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS\n\n37-POINT AUDIT SUMMARY (PASS/FAIL)\nA. Methodology Audit \u2014 PASS (Engine 1 correctly selected; no DCF-only or\n   multiple-only conclusion; scenarios sum to 100%; base case is highest\n   probability).\nB. Valuation Audit \u2014 PASS (WACC derived from observable inputs; \u00b11\u03c3\n   sensitivities shown; top-3 variable tornado; net-debt components declared;\n   no silent terminal-growth ramp).\nC. Bias Audit \u2014 PASS (share-count discrepancy resolved by explicit\n   evidence chain; one-time Q2 gains NOT extrapolated; \u201cAI upside\u201d not in base\n   case; owner-FCF (after SBC) used).\nD. Consistency Audit \u2014 PASS (single T0 reference; FY labels aligned to fiscal\n   year; no mixing of vendor and filed figures without tags).\nE. Narrative Audit \u2014 PASS (no TAM-based valuation; no \u201clarge long-term\n   potential\u201d phrasing).\nF. Red Team Audit \u2014 PASS (7-point short thesis; logic combat scored;\n   adversarial references cited; killed-argument re-arm conditions stated).\nG. Data Integrity Audit \u2014 PASS with disclosures: (i) FY2025 weighted shares vs\n   current shares reconciled; (ii) capex definition discrepancy (ours $0.047B\n   vs vendor $0.105B) embedded in FCF-margin conservatism; (iii) interest\n   expense for FY2024\u201325 not filed \u2192 estimated; (iv) segment-level data absent\n   \u2192 no sum-of-the-parts attempted; (v) DXY/credit-spread/inflation not\n   retrievable \u2192 tagged [Unconfirmed] and reflected in regime probabilities.\nFAILURES: none.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550